  "answer": "The most colorful recipe based on the visual descriptions is **Vegetable Bibimbap** (id=bibimbap). Its caption highlights \"vividly colored arranged piles of orange carrot, green spinach, pale zucchini, dark shiitake, white bean sprouts, a sunny-side-up egg with a glossy orange yolk, and a red dot of gochujang\" – offering the widest variety of bright, contrasting colors. It also fits your vegetarian diet and 30‑minute time limit.",
  "per_turn_responses": [
    "As a vegetarian with about 30 minutes, you have several great options:\n\n- **Avocado Toast** (avocado_toast, 5min) – quick and vegan.\n- **Tomato and Egg Stir-fry** (tomato_egg_stirfry, 8min) – simple and gluten-free.\n- **Miso Soup** (miso_soup, 20min) – warm, vegan, and dairy-free.\n- **Pesto Pasta** (pesto_pasta, 25min) – classic Italian (contains dairy & gluten).\n- **Shakshuka** (shakshuka, 30min) – hearty, gluten-free (contains eggs & dairy).\n- **Vegetable Bibimbap** (bibimbap, 30min) – colorful Korean bowl (contains eggs, soy, sesame).\n\nAll fit your time and dietary preference. Pick one based on your pantry and mood!",
    "Based on your vegetarian diet and 30-minute time limit, you can make any of these:\n\n- Miso Soup (20 min)\n- Pesto Pasta (25 min)\n- Tomato and Egg Stir-fry (8 min)\n- Shakshuka (30 min)\n- Avocado Toast (5 min) – already recommended last time\n- Vegetable Bibimbap (30 min)\n\nAll are ready in 30 minutes or less and are vegetarian-friendly.",
    "The most colorful recipe based on the visual descriptions is **Vegetable Bibimbap** (id=bibimbap). Its caption highlights \"vividly colored arranged piles of orange carrot, green spinach, pale zucchini, dark shiitake, white bean sprouts, a sunny-side-up egg with a glossy orange yolk, and a red dot of gochujang\" – offering the widest variety of bright, contrasting colors. It also fits your vegetarian diet and 30‑minute time limit."
